{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism","id":975846,"title":"Monotheism?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-24T23:08:42-07:00","id":975846,"title":"Monotheism?","content":"I know this is a while big can of worms, but I'm profoundly curious and figure the explosion of activity due to the Kickstarter might lead to some good discussion. How are the major monotheistic faiths handled in Scion, or more accurately how are they handled in <i>your</i> Scion? The Theoi preview mentions that some of the mystery cults have grown to public millions-strong religions by the modern day of The World, and I'm curious to see how (or if) the divergent path the Abrahamic faiths took in the setting's history. While I doubt we'll ever see the Abrahamic Pantheon (I hold out hope that one made up of angels might be the final stretch goal for once of the crowdfunding campaigns), we do know that the Canaanite Pantheon should be on the horizon and that would give us El, who may or may not have become our good friend YHVH in our own real-world theological history. <br /> <br /> Does The World simply give us a henotheistic constellation of Abrahamic faiths, or possibly just have them purge the polytheist elements of Europe and the Near East decidedly less?<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know about the whole Aten mess, but I believe that's been thrown out for 2e.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:22:00-07:00","id":975850,"title":"","content":"It sounds like they just didn't purge as much or their efforts were not nearly as successful.<br /> <br /> Just like I imagine there are plenty of polytheists who believe things which are patently false about their deities who they could actually meet if they were lucky, there's going to be plenty of folks in the World who are comfortably monotheistic because monotheist faiths like Christianity are not exactly relying upon some kind of hard visibility of their deity to derive legitimacy for it.<br /> <br /> Or to think about it another way, when they declare all those pagan gods to be &quot;false idols&quot; it's not in the sense that those beings don't exist, it's in the sense that they are not the one Supreme God who reigns over all things from Heaven. If Zeus tells Joe Christian that's not the case, why is Joe Christian gonna believe him? Because he threw lightning from his hands? Guess who else can do that, Zeus! <i>SATAN!*</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Maybe.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T03:03:32-07:00","id":975896,"title":"","content":"Aten's still playing a part in monotheism, last we heard - specifically exlusionary monotheism, denying the existence of any other gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T07:25:04-07:00","id":975937,"title":"","content":"I hope that the Aten mess will be retconned out. <br /> <br /> So far, it hasn't been a key question in my campaign, and we're kind of ignoring it for now. Since I'm specifically running a Ragnorak campaign, I have even less reason to address it because I don't have to worry about arguments between different pantheons about whose creation story is actually true, now that I think about it. <br /> <br /> I doubt, in any my games, I would have it that one or any of the polytheisms are able to out-do any of the monotheisms. There are compelling sociological arguments for why that is, outside of any supernatural, morality, or spiritual evidence that monotheisms are inherently more widespread and have more 'staying power' (I think that's a fair phrase) than the polytheisms of old. <br /> <br /> Maybe as Ragnorak approaches, and Fimbulwinter sets in, we'll see cults popping up. Hmmmm, not sure. I think I will allow the Band/players decide if there's a revival of worship for the Norse deities, since they'll be the really only big clue that the Aseir are still around. Even then, as Leetsepeak mentions and despite the Band's actions, there's going to be large percentage of the population that will simply disregard any of the Band's claims to divinity and of other divinities for reasons.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm not sure how that interacts with the Legend mechanic, but given how localized the polytheistic deities were, I doubt it takes more than several thousands of people to have the necessary fame and worship to reach godhood from a fluff perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T07:33:04-07:00","id":975938,"title":"","content":"The Scion game I'm running has a very Catholic character, who is a Scion of the Tuatha de Danan. As a GM, I basically treat the Monotheistic gods as they are in the real world. Vague, unknowable, and possibly don't exist at all. Way I see it, the gods and God are not mutually exclusive. You can call Mannanan Mac Lir 'Da' and still do your prayers.<br /> <br /> The only conflict really is what happens to you when you die. I kinda treat it like Heaven and Hell are abstract concepts, rather than actual locations. My player character will probably go to Tir nOg when she dies, but even there, she could 'die' and the gods would have no idea what happens to your soul after that.<br /> <br /> As far as Agen is concerned, I think he's just a liar who has no more knowledge of any 'big G' gods then any of the other deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:40:07-07:00","id":976106,"title":"","content":"Monotheism is extremely easy to explain in both additions settings.<br /> <br /> Fate, the unknowable, at least semi-intelligent force against which even the gods are helpless to fight against? Sounds like a supreme being and the Pantheons are just to full f themselves to admit there's something bigger than them.<br /> <br /> At least that's an easy way for an in character monotheist to think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:45:09-07:00","id":976108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976106#post976106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monotheism is extremely easy to explain in both additions settings.<br /> <br /> Fate, the unknowable, at least semi-intelligent force against which even the gods are helpless to fight against? Sounds like a supreme being and the Pantheons are just to full f themselves to admit there's something bigger than them.<br /> <br /> At least that's an easy way for an in character monotheist to think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of that predicating on knowing all about that magical stuff, which it sounds like most people don't, so it's even easier to have monotheism in the setting because, like in real life, it's not relying on some kind of objective measure of how the world works, but on faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:05:05-07:00","id":976137,"title":"","content":"For the general public yeah, but if you're a Scion who has met Gods, you're going to have to at least adapt to Henotheism... Unless you want to go full delusional and have the character believe all the deities he meets are demons trying to trick him... Which sounds like a reasonable concept for an antagonist.<br /> <br /> But a Henotheist who believes in a One True Highest God/Prime Mover, and all other deities are comparatively lesser functionaries.... Well the Orisha are going to tell you that's explicitly true! The Deva would put it more in Monistic terms of incarnate aspects of the greater whole, rather than intermediaries. The Aesir would just assume you were talking about the Wyrd and let out an exhaserbated sigh. The Theoi would turn you into a duck for suggesting it though - sure their are older forces like Xaos, Nyx, Gaea, and the Titans, but those forces were defeated or kept in their places by the glory of Olympus, and there is no glory greater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-25-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:07:54-07:00","id":976138,"title":"","content":"And honestly, the &quot;gods&quot; aren't exactly a perfect group; they may be demonstratively real and powerful, but that doesn't mean they deserve <b>worship.</b> I'd prefer to put my faith in a deity that <i>isn't</i> inclined to turn into a swan and rape people, thank you very much. Then again, I am somewhat biased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:18:23-07:00","id":976147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976138#post976138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And honestly, the &quot;gods&quot; aren't exactly a perfect group; they may be demonstratively real and powerful, but that doesn't mean they deserve <b>worship.</b> I'd prefer to put my faith in a deity that <i>isn't</i> inclined to turn into a swan and rape people, thank you very much. Then again, I am somewhat biased.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and I think there's real potential in the 'Fate is God' idea. I'm surprised no one has mentioned it before since it fulfills the omnipresent and omnipotent checkboxes and (unless the ST is intent on destroying existence) is benevolent to some degree. <br /> <br /> And I don't think Henotheism is necessary. The polytheistic gods would merely be metaphysical entities of various power levels, but all occupying a lower rung than God/Fate. Or, in the case of a Abrahamic/Angelic Pantheon, the other gods would simply be on the same level as angels and daemons. <br /> <br /> I know the OP was thinking about crafting an Angelic/Abrahamic Pantheon and wanted to ask: how would Scions come to be? 1E was all about the ichor and divine parentage, something that could theoretically happen (given one interpretation of the Nephilim) but is unlikely with the more behaving angels. So, theoretically, if Michael was avoiding sex, how would he have a scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:38:49-07:00","id":976189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976137#post976137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the general public yeah, but if you're a Scion who has met Gods, you're going to have to at least adapt to Henotheism... Unless you want to go full delusional and have the character believe all the deities he meets are demons trying to trick him... Which sounds like a reasonable concept for an antagonist.<br /> <br /> But a Henotheist who believes in a One True Highest God/Prime Mover, and all other deities are comparatively lesser functionaries.... Well the Orisha are going to tell you that's explicitly true! The Deva would put it more in Monistic terms of incarnate aspects of the greater whole, rather than intermediaries. The Aesir would just assume you were talking about the Wyrd and let out an exhaserbated sigh. The Theoi would turn you into a duck for suggesting it though - sure their are older forces like Xaos, Nyx, Gaea, and the Titans, but those forces were defeated or kept in their places by the glory of Olympus, and there is no glory greater.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, although even for the public I think there is going to be more enough factual evidence available in the World that monotheism only makes sense if it is channeled through a Henotheist or Monist lens as you describe. Exclusionary monotheism seems so disproved by evidence that it appears the purview (no pun intended) of a deeply delusional and fanatical mind. Especially because all the other 'demons' seem equally powerful, just as real, and of the same kind as your hypothetic One True God. Well, Aten peddles in that kind of stuff, but unless his personality got radically rewritten, Aten is a megalomanic, delusional loonie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-25-2016, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:53:24-07:00","id":976194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976138#post976138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And honestly, the &quot;gods&quot; aren't exactly a perfect group; they may be demonstratively real and powerful, but that doesn't mean they deserve <b>worship.</b> I'd prefer to put my faith in a deity that <i>isn't</i> inclined to turn into a swan and rape people, thank you very much. Then again, I am somewhat biased.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is worship, and there is worship. Not all kinds of that need be of the kind Abrahamic faiths made our culture familiar with in the last millennium and half. If your gods are demostrably of the powerful but fallible or ethically flawed kind, it may easily be of a more... mercenary and pragmatic, favor-swapping kind: &quot;I give thee this sacrifice, Mighty God, please do me this favor&quot;, or even of the supernatural protection racket kind &quot;I worship thee, Mighty Goddess, please keep illness and bad luck away from me and mine&quot;. If one makes oneself familiar with how religion worked in polytheist or animist cultures, it shows worship was often of this practical kind, and few went around thinking the gods and spirits were safe or wise to ignore or slight simply because they weren't always benevolent or morally upstanding. From a pragmatic PoV, since in the Scion setting nothing suggests it would be feasible for mortals to make war against the Pantheons, it may be the preferable choice for most to try and get in the good grace of more powerful, untouchable entities even if they fancy to play fast and loose with consent in their many one-night-stands or lay down disproportionate retribution for petty slights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-25-2016, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T18:33:44-07:00","id":976217,"title":"","content":"I've always played it like Fate is God, but also I took a nod from Riordan and have the gods themselves not know the answer to it (Tyche I think is Buddhist in the Olympian novels). There's a joke in my game that Thor's been a ardent catholic since the 11th century, pissing off his dad and uncle to no end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:04:24-07:00","id":976243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976217#post976217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always played it like Fate is God, but also I took a nod from Riordan and have the gods themselves not know the answer to it (Tyche I think is Buddhist in the Olympian novels). There's a joke in my game that Thor's been a ardent catholic since the 11th century, pissing off his dad and uncle to no end.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *tries to imagine Thor as a Catholic*<br /> <br /> ...that's hilarious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:48:46-07:00","id":976367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=975850#post975850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like they just didn't purge as much or their efforts were not nearly as successful.<br /> <br /> Just like I imagine there are plenty of polytheists who believe things which are patently false about their deities who they could actually meet if they were lucky, there's going to be plenty of folks in the World who are comfortably monotheistic because monotheist faiths like Christianity are not exactly relying upon some kind of hard visibility of their deity to derive legitimacy for it.<br /> <br /> Or to think about it another way, when they declare all those pagan gods to be &quot;false idols&quot; it's not in the sense that those beings don't exist, it's in the sense that they are not the one Supreme God who reigns over all things from Heaven. If Zeus tells Joe Christian that's not the case, why is Joe Christian gonna believe him? Because he threw lightning from his hands? Guess who else can do that, Zeus! <i>SATAN!*</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Maybe.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The key factor is that He is King of Kings - and more appropriately for the setting , God of Gods. God isn't making Scions, every baptized Christian is a Scion due to being Christ's adopted brother or sister. No, he's sanctifying Saints, Prophets, Missionaries - people to live his Word and to but the bug in the ear of the other Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:59:07-07:00","id":976375,"title":"","content":"As settings go, it would be fairly ridiculous to grant Christianity primacy over other religions and pantheons in Scion. One of the most baseline assumptions of the Christian faith is downright wrong: That there is only one true god.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that nothing is there? No, of course not. Does it mean that anyone is truly the King of Kings? Probably not. Does it mean that anyone is the God of Gods? Oh hell no. Does that mean no one can believe these things? Of course not. People believe all kinds of things, even when they're not true.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:00:57-07:00","id":976376,"title":"","content":"There is a reference in the most recent setting update to the Knights Templar having gone to war against polytheism. Obviously the Teutonic Knights would have been more accurate, but I get that the Templar name carries the greater genre fiction cache.<br /> <br /> So there were purge/force conversion attempts, but they weren't as overwhelming as in our European (and presumably West Asian) history.<br /> <br /> For example, I would imagine Cromwell was pretty bad for pagans in England and Ireland along with Catholics. The Restoration would have seen oppression of both greatly relax, while the Glorious Revolution routed Tuatha worshippers and other Celtic pagans along with Catholics, BUT was largely accepting of Anglo-Saxon (/Dutch) Aesir worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:14:53-07:00","id":976382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976375#post976375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As settings go, it would be fairly ridiculous to grant Christianity primacy over other religions and pantheons in Scion. One of the most baseline assumptions of the Christian faith is downright wrong: That there is only one true god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a verifiable measuring stick for what is or isn't a God that you could show to objectively prove to them that the divinities of the Theoi or the Yazata actually merit the description of God? Is the notion of God contingent upon evidence in the first place? And is the suggestion seeded anywhere to suggest that Christianity has some primacy among the religions of The World? Everything points to this not necessarily being the case. It doesn't mean Christianity is so much less influential, rather that it is one among a number of large, prominent faiths in the world.<br /> <br /> Is the baseline assumption of Christianity correct in our world? Can you say? Would the presence of powerful, mysterious beings from another world who can do things that are wonderous necessarily disprove that?<br /> <br /> Would the existence of aliens disprove the existence of God?<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, it's being discussed as if there's a binary of One God or All Gods, and that seems to be contingent upon the Christian Faith acknowledging those other gods <i>as gods</i>. Why would they? They say they're not Gods in real life, and just because some big scary man shows up and says he IS a god and bullies you doesn't mean you'll believe he's a god. You'll probably believe he's a bully and not a very good person to worship if he does that, which might play right into the hands of an antagonistic monotheist worldview.<br /> <br /> And that's all contingent on Zeus making press conferences on the state of the Eleusinian Mysteries, which evidently is <i>not </i>the default situation of The World.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:26:04-07:00","id":976388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976382#post976382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a verifiable measuring stick for what is or isn't a God that you could show to objectively prove to them that the divinities of the Theoi or the Yazata actually merit the description of God? Is the notion of God contingent upon evidence in the first place? And is the suggestion seeded anywhere to suggest that Christianity has some primacy among the religions of The World? Everything points to this not necessarily being the case. It doesn't mean Christianity is so much less influential, rather that it is one among a number of large, prominent faiths in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're shifting the goalposts and asking me to defend arguments I never made. I think that as far as the Scion setting goes, pantheons are composed of actual gods. What people believe in the actual setting itself is not relevant because we're not talking about their beliefs but about how the world is constituted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976382#post976382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the baseline assumption of Christianity correct in our world? Can you say? Would the presence of powerful, mysterious beings from another world who can do things that are wonderous necessarily disprove that?<br /> <br /> Would the existence of aliens disprove the existence of God?</div> </div> </div> </div>These questions are completely irrelevant to the discussion. We're not talking about our world, we're talking about possible interpretations of the world as represented in Scion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976382#post976382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying, it's being discussed as if there's a binary of One God or All Gods, and that seems to be contingent upon the Christian Faith acknowledging those other gods <i>as gods</i>. Why would they? They say they're not Gods in real life, and just because some big scary man shows up and says he IS a god and bullies you doesn't mean you'll believe he's a god. You'll probably believe he's a bully and not a very good person to worship if he does that, which might play right into the hands of an antagonistic monotheist worldview.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about what the Christian faith would do or not do, or what the various actual gods in Scion's setting would do. Read the post immediately before mine and perhaps context will clarify my intention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976382#post976382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's all contingent on Zeus making press conferences on the state of the Eleusinian Mysteries, which evidently is <i>not </i>the default situation of The World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing I said was contingent on Zeus doing literally anything.<br /> <br /> Seriously, just read the post right before mine and read mine in that context. My intended meaning should be quite clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:11:41-07:00","id":976401,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, seems like you were having a different discussion than me. The way the World is metaphysically constructed has very little bearing on how people might choose to affiliate religiously, that's the thing I was getting at, which is how you wind up with the Eleusinian Mysteries still being practiced alongside Christianity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T05:42:12-07:00","id":976479,"title":"","content":"Monotheism is about power and social order. Strict commandments, punishing heretics, unifying society to focus worship of one deity, lbmaking it far easier to control how they was worship and what, then a hodge podge of deities, each with their own values and traditions, and symbols, and hertiage, much easier to control a population when you control the religion absulotely.<br /> <br /> So I'd have certain Gods/Pantheons, backing certain monotheistic religions as a power grab basically, an attempt to manipulate people and society, so they'd be power behind the church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:27:53-07:00","id":976537,"title":"","content":"I have treated this issue in my games as one of Belief vs Faith.<br /> <br /> It is easy to believe in various gods like Zeus, Tlaloc, etc when they and their scions are bounding about and displaying magical abilities.<br /> <br /> It takes faith to worship a deity that does not directly intercede, especially when there are others that do so almost too readily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:25:35-07:00","id":976562,"title":"","content":"Speaking less about faith and more about history in our world, even the Abrahamic religions were only 'sorta monotheistic' in the very early days. In a fictional world where gods are real, YHWH may just be the last member of it's pantheon still standing, with the others having been lost long ago. Attribute whatever reasons you want to that, from YHWH being a jealous god who won't let anyone be worshipped before him, or titans taking out the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:34:48-07:00","id":976568,"title":"","content":"If I had to say it for my table, The World has just as many angels as it does satyrs and jotun and what have you, and while YHVH only has one Born Scion on the books, either He or His subservient Pantheon of archangels are more than happy to choose servants as much as any other. I just think that Onyx Path rightly wants to steer away from that giant mess of controversy that such a thing would entail in their predominantly Abrahamic-culturally Western world. I would be stunned (but overjoyed!) if we ever saw anything official beyond &quot;those faiths exist in The World, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I think the Canaanite Pantheon is an incredibly clever way of tackling the subject. It would be much easier to say &quot;maybe El or an aspect of him breaks away from the others of his Pantheon and is revered by mortal followers as the greatest among all gods and thus the only one worthy of worship.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:54:05-07:00","id":976584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976568#post976568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to say it for my table, The World has just as many angels as it does satyrs and jotun and what have you, and while YHVH only has one Born Scion on the books, either He or His subservient Pantheon of archangels are more than happy to choose servants as much as any other. I just think that Onyx Path rightly wants to steer away from that giant mess of controversy that such a thing would entail in their predominantly Abrahamic-culturally Western world. I would be stunned (but overjoyed!) if we ever saw anything official beyond &quot;those faiths exist in The World, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I think the Canaanite Pantheon is an incredibly clever way of tackling the subject. It would be much easier to say &quot;maybe El or an aspect of him breaks away from the others of his Pantheon and is revered by mortal followers as the greatest among all gods and thus the only one worthy of worship.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And the more practical question I posed a page or two ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:02:46-07:00","id":976680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976584#post976584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And the more practical question I posed a page or two ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>About where you get Angelic Scions from? I would assume they would likely focus on Chosen and Incarnate Scions (trying to Create one would be prideful, as I'd assume that's solely the domain of the Lord), though you might get some Born Scions via the Nephilim route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:08:17-07:00","id":976687,"title":"","content":"Fair answer. And who would be on the roster? I would assume Gabriel and Michael, since they are directly mentioned in the Old Testament. Rapheal is mentioned in the Book of Enoch. The or a Cherubim guards the Garden. That's four right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:13:14-07:00","id":976690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976687#post976687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair answer. And who would be on the roster? I would assume Gabriel and Michael, since they are directly mentioned in the Old Testament. Rapheal is mentioned in the Book of Enoch. The or a Cherubim guards the Garden. That's four right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>We usually get seven archangels, though sources argue about who those seven all are. Uriel obviously deserves a spot, I'm a big fan of Ramiel, and you might as well toss Metatron in there.<br /> <br /> I have to find a place for summoning the Merkabah chariot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:21:39-07:00","id":976697,"title":"","content":"So, 7. I think 12 is the standard number for a 'full' pantheon? I'm not sure the 4 four-headed angels around the throne would count since they're anchored. I suppose you could make up a couple of Nephilim to round out the roster, or children of the Nephilim to get some women into the pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:23:05-07:00","id":976698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976697#post976697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, 7. I think 12 is the standard number for a 'full' pantheon? I'm not sure the 4 four-headed angels around the throne would count since they're anchored. I suppose you could make up a couple of Nephilim to round out the roster, or children of the Nephilim to get some women into the pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a schism between the angels of the old texts and the angels of later occult traditions, or go the obvious route and have a handful of fallen angels in the mix who are nontheless still divine and potent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:33:38-07:00","id":976705,"title":"","content":"Or both. Have three different factions among the Pantheon, but who are mostly on the same side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:15:03-07:00","id":976750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976687#post976687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair answer. And who would be on the roster? I would assume Gabriel and Michael, since they are directly mentioned in the Old Testament. Rapheal is mentioned in the Book of Enoch. The or a Cherubim guards the Garden. That's four right there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anyone who's read the Dresden Files knows that Uriel is an obvious choice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, would the Devil also be part of the Abrahamic pantheon? Scions of Lucifer would certainly be fun, particularly if they're basically good people. You could use films like The Devils Advocate with Keanu Reeves and Al Pacino as inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:57:45-07:00","id":976847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976750#post976750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anyone who's read the Dresden Files knows that Uriel is an obvious choice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, would the Devil also be part of the Abrahamic pantheon? Scions of Lucifer would certainly be fun, particularly if they're basically good people. You could use films like The Devils Advocate with Keanu Reeves and Al Pacino as inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think any halfway proper Scion game would be clever enough to draw the distinction between the fallen angel Lucifer and the actual demonic Adversary, though mortal Fatebindings confusing the two might make for interesting story fodder. I think our pal the Morningstar has a place somewhere in the mix, especially given how heavily 2e draws on <i>WicDiv </i>for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:43:37-07:00","id":976865,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, I am not at all familiar with the Christian Faith, how unique is each angel, how are they depicted in myth, do they have genders, and how do they interact in the divine community?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:14:57-07:00","id":976881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976865#post976865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, I am not at all familiar with the Christian Faith, how unique is each angel, how are they depicted in myth, do they have genders, and how do they interact in the divine community?</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels do not have sexes, some are not even humanoid (wheels of fire covered in eyes and wings) and the uniqueness of Angels is a bit of a toss up. There are theoretical legions of almost nameless ones, but the bigger important ones of various branches of Angelic beings tend to be named. What do you mean by the divine community though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:01:12-07:00","id":976900,"title":"","content":"I assume it's a question of what their relationships are with one another.<br /> <br /> I think the answer is not much. Which might be part of why the notion of an angelic pantheon is perhaps less interesting in practice than in theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:08:23-07:00","id":976903,"title":"","content":"A lot's been done with angels in popular culture so there's definitely room for interesting takes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:16:43-07:00","id":976908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976900#post976900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume it's a question of what their relationships are with one another.<br /> <br /> I think the answer is not much. Which might be part of why the notion of an angelic pantheon is perhaps less interesting in practice than in theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, yes I meant with each other, I saw some names of angels in this thread and they sounded male to me. So are there no personal relationships between say Uriel and Michael (I don't know them at all so forgive my ignorance)?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps they are not meant to be relatable by human beings. If that's the case, playing a scion of an angel would be like playing something trying to interlocute between angels and humans, that sounds interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:32:44-07:00","id":976916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976900#post976900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume it's a question of what their relationships are with one another.<br /> <br /> I think the answer is not much. Which might be part of why the notion of an angelic pantheon is perhaps less interesting in practice than in theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels are (and would be, in a Pantheon) defined by their service to YHVH/God/Allah/etc, rather than strife between each other (fallen angels notwithstanding); the take I'm imagining for the archangels would be more focused on what they do left to their own devices when they stop 'receiving orders' as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T21:07:03-07:00","id":976928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976916#post976916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Angels are (and would be, in a Pantheon) defined by their service to YHVH/God/Allah/etc, rather than strife between each other (fallen angels notwithstanding); the take I'm imagining for the archangels would be more focused on what they do left to their own devices when they stop 'receiving orders' as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you <i>really</i> want to make a pantheon of the Archangels, you have no further to look than the obscure game <b>In Nomine</b>. All your associations, purviews, attitudes, etc are laid out for you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I avoided the whole issue of Abrahamic monotheism in my Scion 1E game by simply negating it's relevancy. The last person to create exclusionary montheism started the whole mess that led to Aten, so it was just as well that any other attempt met the same end. Equating the being described as &quot;YHVH/God&quot; with Fate is cute when you consider that Fate shares a lot of the same attributes; Omnipotence, Omnipresence, Non-verifiable Omniscience, An incomprehensibly alien level of distance from the day to day, and neutral bias that may not synch up with the flock's assumption of beneficence. Praying to Fate with the assumption that it is the equivalent of &quot;YHVH/God&quot; is pretty much like praying to your dice for a nat 20, with less odds of it actually working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:22:30-07:00","id":977394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=976243#post976243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> *tries to imagine Thor as a Catholic*<br /> <br /> ...that's hilarious!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy Scion games are often pretty heavily tongue in cheek.<br /> <br /> Hell we even once had a scion of Sun Wukong who was Neil Patrick Harris. Not &quot;Using Neil as a character model&quot; but actually Neil Patrick Harris, Neil Patrick Harris Killed Hogzilla with a Prius in his introduction scene.<br /> <br /> that was different.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the reasons I'm so excited about 2e is that I get to run a non-gonzo story. My usual games are pretty heavy on the horror and I'm pretty good at building tension but I've never done either in a scion game (save once but we all decided that we'd had enough of the system by then) so my players are really nervous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":". 09-27-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:53:35-07:00","id":977414,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it was a fun game. <br /> <br /> What's a 'non-gonzo' game?<br /> <br /> Regarding the original topic, the roster sounds like...<br /> Michael<br /> Gabriel<br /> Lucifer<br /> Raphael<br /> Uriel<br /> Ramiel<br /> Raguel<br /> Sariel<br /> Metatron<br /> <br /> That's 9. The first three are mentioned in the Bible proper, while the next five are listed in the Book of Enoch. Metatron is more of a mystery and seems more tied to the Talmud. Reviewing the original Scion game, the pantheons ranged from 12 at the most to as little as 7. So, technically, you have a full roster right there. There is another list that has Jophiel, Zadkiel, and Camael for other additions or alternate names for the first nine. And, of course, more could be added, either from In Nominee or just coming up with more on your own. <br /> <br /> How you handle the relationships between each other and humanity would depend on the ST. One could go the 'too strange for mortal minds' route. In the Bible, half the time an angel appeared, they had to say 'chill out' because they tended to freak out people with their arrival. Not to mention the angels who defy physics with their forms.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's also possible to make them much more relatable. There are also plenty of recorded instances where angels came in and nobody could tell the difference between an angel and a typical person. So, perhaps the angels do have pretty typical relationships between each other. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:01:15-07:00","id":977444,"title":"","content":"Gonzo games are over the top, often intense, usually silly games that, while fun and cool are rarely moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:09:06-07:00","id":977452,"title":"","content":"Gotcha. Right now, it looks like my Norse game is heading towards Gonzo, though I would like for it to have some serious moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:09:48-07:00","id":977453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=977394#post977394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bMy Scion games are often pretty heavily tongue in cheek.<br /> <br /> Hell we even once had a scion of Sun Wukong who was Neil Patrick Harris. Not &quot;Using Neil as a character model&quot; but actually Neil Patrick Harris, Neil Patrick Harris Killed Hogzilla with a Prius in his introduction scene.<br /> <br /> that was different.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne of the reasons I'm so excited about 2e is that I get to run a non-gonzo story. My usual games are pretty heavy on the horror and I'm pretty good at building tension but I've never done either in a scion game (save once but we all decided that we'd had enough of the system by then) so my players are really nervous.</div> </div> </div> </div>So was Sun Wukong playing a prank on his son by trapping him in a contract to play Doogie Howser?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:35:56-07:00","id":977466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=977453#post977453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So was Sun Wukong playing a prank on his son by trapping him in a contract to play Doogie Howser?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou're taste in quality entertainment is bad and you should feel bad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T17:06:46-07:00","id":977484,"title":"","content":"Hey now, I never said anything about quality. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:06:33-07:00","id":992772,"title":"","content":"An idea: Maybe YHVH/God/Allah is a Mantle of El that's grown too big for His almighty britches or maybe He's always been a one-man Pantheon, but the origin story really doesn't matter here. What <i>does</i> matter is that wherever He comes from, he's alone now, and thus has no one to hoist His Fatebindings off onto; any ripple He creates comes straight back around and slaps Him square in the face. So He's retreated from the World, handing out less and less miracles (and really learning His lesson after what happened to His one poor Born scion), and now rarely passes out Relics and makes very scarce Chosen scions, because to do anything more shackles Him even further than several thousand years of contradictory theology spread across three millions-strong faiths already does.<br /> <br /> Heck, this is probably why the homebrew Pantheon of Archangels I've been sitting on exists: His hands are too tied to do anything, so he has helpers do it all for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 10-25-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:38:34-07:00","id":992786,"title":"","content":"Aren't we getting both the Caananites and pre-Islam Arabic pantheons each potentially? El and Allah seem like they'd be different gods, unless this becomes an example of a god who can bounce between pantheons rather than mantles within the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:02:20-07:00","id":992794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992786#post992786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't we getting both the Caananites and pre-Islam Arabic pantheons each potentially? El and Allah seem like they'd be different gods, unless this becomes an example of a god who can bounce between pantheons rather than mantles within the same</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't heard anything about an Arabic Pantheon, and I doubt delving into Alilat the moon goddess is going to win the Scion team any friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:05:54-07:00","id":992796,"title":"","content":"I've been lurking here for a while and could easily be drunkenly mixing shit up in my head from fan musing rather than official statements or at least chatter from writers. Like I really distinctly remember this in the Ask Neall thread or something, but as I search around I'm not spying anything. So I guess I imagined it all, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:12:01-07:00","id":992799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992796#post992796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been lurking here for a while and could easily be drunkenly mixing shit up in my head from fan musing rather than official statements or at least chatter from writers. Like I really distinctly remember this in the Ask Neall thread or something, but as I search around I'm not spying anything. So I guess I imagined it all, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a bit where DaveB said it's good he wasn't in charge because he <i>would</i> cover that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:16:57-07:00","id":992801,"title":"","content":"Maybe that. Looks like I raised my hopes for nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:38:23-07:00","id":992811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992801#post992801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that. Looks like I raised my hopes for nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canaanite should still be in as a Demigod stretch goal along with the Welsh, with the Mayan, Navajo, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, and Slavic in that corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:38:23-07:00","id":992812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992801#post992801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe that. Looks like I raised my hopes for nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canaanite should still be in as a Demigod stretch goal along with the Welsh, with the Mayan, Navajo, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, and Slavic in that corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:47:19-07:00","id":992817,"title":"","content":"The issue is that even monotheistic religions tend not to be monotheistic. Protestant Christians have the Holy Trinity, Catholics in Italy pray more often to saints than they do Jesus himself, the old testament allows for the existence of other gods, you're just not supposed to worship them - and of course, the further back you go the more divergent it gets, with a queen of heaven and other more minor gods. <br /> <br /> As far as angels go, I'd never use them at my table. They are generally speaking obsessed with the Order of the universe yes - but in a bizarre twist of irony, in Scion they are titans. Neall has specifically mentioned that Titans are entities that get really carried away with their purviews, claiming that Prometheus didn't give man fire out of the goodness of his heart, he 'needed' to spread it. Add to this that we have a mirror in Lucifer, or with Satan tempting man to eat the fruit from the tree of knowledge, and angels almost exclusively parallel with titans in other mythologies. <br /> <br /> Also we already have angelic scions, the Nephilim. They are the children of angels and humans, and are described as giants, often monstrous, etc. I don't see any chance of an official angelic pantheon coming about in light of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:48:03-07:00","id":992818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992811#post992811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Canaanite should still be in as a Demigod stretch goal along with the Welsh, with the Mayan, Navajo, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, and Slavic in that corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I believe from last we heard from Neall on the subject, the Elohim were most likely in God, and the Welsh Pantheon was planned for a supplement focusing on Arthurian Myth-Cycle.<br /> <br /> Mayan, Navajo, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, and Slavic are indeed planned for Demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:58:00-07:00","id":992824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992818#post992818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually I believe from last we heard from Neall on the subject, the Elohim were most likely in God, and the Welsh Pantheon was planned for a supplement focusing on Arthurian Myth-Cycle.<br /> <br /> Mayan, Navajo, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, and Slavic are indeed planned for Demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall was still deciding between Mayan and Incan, last he mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:58:48-07:00","id":992826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992818#post992818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually I believe from last we heard from Neall on the subject, the Elohim were most likely in God, and the Welsh Pantheon was planned for a supplement focusing on Arthurian Myth-Cycle.<br /> <br /> Mayan, Navajo, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, and Slavic are indeed planned for Demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for quote-mining, but as someone who wants both ASAP this is what I could find to give me hope:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626576#post626576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aten is something that's going to be in the book, just different. The Caananite pantheon is something I'd like to cover in Scion anyways, warily circling the Egyptian and Mesopotamian pantheons in a Levantine standoff. They're slated for the Demigod book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968776#post968776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, I'd like to have the Nemetondevos, Loa, and Yazata as stretch goals. So, 2.5 pantheons.<br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b>'s current slate is the Mespotamia, Mayan, Polynesian, Slavic, and Navajo pantheons. I'd <i>really</i> like to do the Welsh pantheon in a larger <b>Demigod</b>-era book of Arthurian myth. I'm also considering Lakota, Caananite, and Guarani for other supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:59:36-07:00","id":992827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992824#post992824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neall was still deciding between Mayan and Incan, last he mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope he chooses Incan, because if Mayan is left out I am hitting that Pantheon book for Community Release like a god damned hurricane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:25:07-07:00","id":992836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992826#post992826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apologies for quote-mining, but as someone who wants both ASAP this is what I could find to give me hope:</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;a larger Demigod-era book&quot; means a different era book. He's explicitly refering to it as being in a separate book from the Mesopotamian, Mayan, Polynesian, and Slavic Pantheons. Also note that &quot;Demigod's current slate&quot; does not include the Elohim in the more recent quote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:46:46-07:00","id":992987,"title":"","content":"To be quite honest, I've got no idea, myself, how the World could remotely resemble ours. If the gods send a Scion to the Aztecs on the eve of the arrival of the conquidtadores, I don't think any amount of guns, germs, or steel will save you. If the gods regularly send epic heroes into the world, who reshape it casually in their passing, how is anyone to deny their existence? Primacy, perhaps, but existence?<br /> <br /> And that's without even touching the Enlightenment and scientific revolution being backed by more deist lines of thinking about Nature and Nature's God.<br /> <br /> There is, to my mind, no causal skein of history that'd leave the World looking quite like our world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:33:18-07:00","id":993041,"title":"","content":"I mean I am too fond of the Loa to make Monotheism just Fate or an unknowable. The truth is many Polytheistic religions have inclinations toward a larger being. So Monotheism's definitely a Real thing when I play, but that's the thing.<br /> <br /> I kind of play them as a God of Gods and while mortals can get glimpses and signs of a bigger god, they often misunderstand or misconstrue. I mean look how varied Egyptian Gods are over a period of years and cultures. Now add the entire history of the Earth and all the cultures there-of. People misinterpret God all the time. <br /> <br /> Monotheism is worshiping that source, believing the other gods to be the equivalent of powerful spirits/demons/Angels/ and even forms God takes similar when a god reincarnates into a human, but with God they take the form of a &quot;new&quot; god, giving them individuality and sentience when they do so. Some Pantheons even support this theory, believing themselves to be powerful entities in service to a larger one. Others do not.<br /> <br /> In any case, there is enough evidence that being a Monotheist is not impossible or delusional. God works in mysterious ways, and the idea of a &quot;King of Kings&quot; is not lost on even a scion. Your parents are strong and powerful, no doubt, but no stronger than a D'jinn or an Angel, or a powerful Spirit. Of course that doesn't mean anything else about their powers. And you can still help/fight/serve as a scion. It just means your prayers go to someone else, someone more powerful than all of them combined. It's a hell of a lot less personal and sometimes you doubt if He's listening, but few gods would ever call it crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:44:09-07:00","id":993048,"title":"","content":"I don't find the idea of playing Scion in a Christian-centric universe to be appealing at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-25-2016, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T12:48:44-07:00","id":993050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=992987#post992987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be quite honest, I've got no idea, myself, how the World could remotely resemble ours. If the gods send a Scion to the Aztecs on the eve of the arrival of the conquidtadores, I don't think any amount of guns, germs, or steel will save you. If the gods regularly send epic heroes into the world, who reshape it casually in their passing, how is anyone to deny their existence? Primacy, perhaps, but existence?<br /> <br /> And that's without even touching the Enlightenment and scientific revolution being backed by more deist lines of thinking about Nature and Nature's God.<br /> <br /> There is, to my mind, no causal skein of history that'd leave the World looking quite like our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>How regular is regular though? 10 or so a generation? Which becomes a much smaller ratio as population grows, and similarly, less mythical events &quot;happen&quot;. And even then most scions never reach demi-god level, they instead become our De Vincis, our Hannibals, or our Beethovens. They are on the winning side of battles like Agincourt or New Orleans 1812. They are impressive and might alter events, but only a few will be known by more than a few hundred people. The core element here is that while there aren\u2019t any hard rules about not showing yourself, most tend to avoid the nasty fate entanglements, most periods of history don\u2019t have many, and most of those probably fade into folktales and urban legends. I think it is fairly easy to recontextualise events as \u201cthere was one at the one historical event\u201d well \u201cmaybe opposing ones canceled each other out\u201d, \u201cPantheon X didn\u2019t want to provoke a war with Pantheon y\u201d, \u201cNo one believed the witnesses\u201d, amd other perfectly believable excuses. If we assume that the cold war Neil has talked about has only been ramping up over the past couple decades than history probably wouldn\u2019t be massively changed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:07:58-07:00","id":993057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993048#post993048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably take my gaming elsewhere if faced with that kind of thing in a Scion game. It undermines a lot of what Scion is, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it's the baseline Scion.<br /> <br /> I mean I'm mostly an atheist, but I'm not saying God shows up a lot (in fact, the entity should <i><b>never</b></i> show up), just that you can believe in Monotheism and not be crazy and actual myths recognize that there are higher beings beyond Gods in several mythologies, so it is also mythologically compatible. It's not a started fact (except in some religions, like the Loa) but I haven't changed anything in the setting. Unless a player chose to be part of the Loa, or character was Monotheistic themselves, it would never come up.<br /> <br /> No way is monotheism not real if it is wide spread. I mean the Gods would have squashed it and it would feel unrealistic. But if there is a subtle power that keeps foiling them, or they see it as a viable religion they can at least respect (in the case of some religions) then that is the only way I can see the world ending up as it is in the setting while being mythologically compatible. Either Monotheism does not exist or God exists, and I tried to capture that as close to what other mythologies allowed since the base setting says Monotheism is still around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:22:01-07:00","id":993069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993057#post993057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me it's the baseline Scion.<br /> <br /> I mean I'm mostly an atheist, but I'm not saying God shows up a lot (in fact, the entity should <i><b>never</b></i> show up), just that you can believe in Monotheism and not be crazy and actual myths recognize that there are higher beings beyond Gods in several mythologies, so it is also mythologically compatible. It's not a started fact (except in some religions, like the Loa) but I haven't changed anything in the setting. Unless a player chose to be part of the Loa, or character was Monotheistic themselves, it would never come up.<br /> <br /> No way is monotheism not real if it is wide spread. I mean the Gods would have squashed it and it would feel unrealistic. But if there is a subtle power that keeps foiling them, or they see it as a viable religion they can at least respect (in the case of some religions) then that is the only way I can see the world ending up as it is in the setting while being mythologically compatible. Either Monotheism does not exist or God exists, and I tried to capture that as close to what other mythologies allowed since the base setting says Monotheism is still around.</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it more explicitly: I don't see the appeal in making Christianity a special religion above all others. That's <i>not</i> the baseline Scion at all. Baseline Scion says all myths are true and presents numerous pantheons as having relatively equivalent cosmological meaning and power. The existence of each pantheon is proof that monotheism isn't real in Scion. There is nothing in Scion that implies, suggests, states, or asserts that the Christian god is the most powerful, and Neall basically described monotheism as an attempt to screw over the pantheons.<br /> <br /> Making monotheism real and placing the Christian god above all others would spoil Scion's flavor. It turns the game into something it isn't, and IMO something that it shouldn't be. I would rather see first edition Aten return than see anything supporting what you wrote, and I don't want to see first edition Aten return, either.<br /> <br /> IMO, in Scion, monotheism does <i>not</i> exist and no god or pantheon wields supremacy over all others. If that means god doesn't exist, c'est la vie. I don't think it does, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:43:54-07:00","id":993078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993069#post993069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Christian god</div> </div> </div> </div>Same God for Jews and Islam, fam. No need to tip your fedora<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993069#post993069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">placing the Christian god above all others</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is doing that. If it were in Scion, it wouldn't be special. It'd be a religion in Scion with their deity in Scion. <br /> <br /> .<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993069#post993069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of each pantheon is proof that monotheism isn't real in Scion</div> </div> </div> </div>Beginning of your post you said &quot;Baseline Scion says all myths are true&quot;.<br /> <br /> All creations myths contradict each other, but the Abrahamic pantheon can't have theirs because it would contradict the others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:45:28-07:00","id":993079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993069#post993069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To put it more explicitly: I don't see the appeal in making Christianity a special religion above all others. That's <i>not</i> the baseline Scion at all. Baseline Scion says all myths are true and presents numerous pantheons as having relatively equivalent cosmological meaning and power. The existence of each pantheon is proof that monotheism isn't real in Scion. There is nothing in Scion that implies, suggests, states, or asserts that the Christian god is the most powerful, and Neall basically described monotheism as an attempt to screw over the pantheons.<br /> <br /> Making monotheism real and placing the Christian god above all others would spoil Scion's flavor. It turns the game into something it isn't, and IMO something that it shouldn't be. I would rather see first edition Aten return than see anything supporting what you wrote, and I don't want to see first edition Aten return, either.<br /> <br /> IMO, in Scion, monotheism does <i>not</i> exist and no god or pantheon wields supremacy over all others. If that means god doesn't exist, c'est la vie. I don't think it does, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I feel I've angered you and that was not my point, I apologize, let me try to explain. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Monotheism does exist in the setting as a faith, I mean they said Monotheism is just a bit smaller than it is now with big Jesus statues and everything. I am trying to balance that with myths, cause without a god to back them up, well monotheism just wouldn't be in a world where gods exist. I tried to make it clear that Christians/Jews/and Muslims interpreted this being wrong, and I in no way tried to imply that Christianity is the be all/end all and very much think I lumped each Abrahamic faith together somewhat slovenly if nothing else. Just wanted to figure out how monotheism exists. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For me Monotheistic religions are just other mythologies and I'm trying to be faithful to them too in a setting that acknowledges that people believe in those things. But no one gets any powers from them, Christianity/Islam/ and Judaism is considered a frail mortal interpretation of a Divinity that only a few Pantheons recognize. I thought I balanced it very clearly toward polytheistic viewpoints. Also I've always been fascinated by different mythologies that had higher forces and wanted to tie that into the setting so there is an explanation, rather than saying my favorite Pantheon is crazy or ignoring it entirely. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I am definitely not a Christian trying to say Christianity is best, just a bit of an arm chair mythologist trying to make it make sense but I want this to be a fun discussion, and I'll stop if you want.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:02:50-07:00","id":993088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993078#post993078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same God for Jews and Islam, fam. <b>No need to tip your fedora</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What does this even mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993078#post993078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is doing that. If it were in Scion, it wouldn't be special. It'd be a religion in Scion with their deity in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>.Re-read 3comrades' post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, there is enough evidence that being a Monotheist is not impossible or delusional. God works in mysterious ways, and the idea of a &quot;King of Kings&quot; is not lost on even a scion. <b>Your parents are strong and powerful, no doubt, but no stronger than a D'jinn or an Angel, or a powerful Spirit. </b>Of course that doesn't mean anything else about their powers. And you can still help/fight/serve as a scion.<b> It just means your prayers go to someone else, someone more powerful than all of them combined.</b> It's a hell of a lot less personal and sometimes you doubt if He's listening, but few gods would ever call it crazy. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993078#post993078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beginning of your post you said &quot;Baseline Scion says all myths are true&quot;.<br /> <br /> All creations myths contradict each other, but the Abrahamic pantheon can't have theirs because it would contradict the others?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that the Abrahamic pantheon can't have their creation myth. I said that making the Abrahamic pantheon more powerful than all others combined shouldn't happen, and that all the other gods in all the other pantheons shouldn't simply be equal to angels and djinni. The reason I pointed out that &quot;all myths are true&quot; is because I disagree with making some myths <i>far more true</i> than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-25-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:07:58-07:00","id":993090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993079#post993079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I feel I've angered you and that was not my point, I apologize, let me try to explain. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Monotheism does exist in the setting as a faith, I mean they said Monotheism is just a bit smaller than it is now with big Jesus statues and everything. I am trying to balance that with myths, cause without a god to back them up, well monotheism just wouldn't be in a world where gods exist. I tried to make it clear that Christians/Jews/and Muslims interpreted this being wrong, and I in no way tried to imply that Christianity is the be all/end all and very much think I lumped each Abrahamic faith together somewhat slovenly if nothing else. Just wanted to figure out how monotheism exists. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For me Monotheistic religions are just other mythologies and I'm trying to be faithful to them too in a setting that acknowledges that people believe in those things. But no one gets any powers from them, Christianity/Islam/ and Judaism is considered a frail mortal interpretation of a Divinity that only a few Pantheons recognize. I thought I balanced it very clearly toward polytheistic viewpoints. Also I've always been fascinated by different mythologies that had higher forces and wanted to tie that into the setting so there is an explanation, rather than saying my favorite Pantheon is crazy or ignoring it entirely. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I am definitely not a Christian trying to say Christianity is best, just a bit of an arm chair mythologist trying to make it make sense but I want this to be a fun discussion, and I'll stop if you want.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not angry, and I am sorry I came across as such. I just disagreed a bit vehemently to what you said.<br /> <br /> What I specifically objected to was the whole bit here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your parents are strong and powerful, no doubt, but no stronger than a D'jinn or an Angel, or a powerful Spirit. Of course that doesn't mean anything else about their powers. And you can still help/fight/serve as a scion. It just means your prayers go to someone else, someone more powerful than all of them combined. </div> </div> </div>Setting out to make the gods of the various pantheons relatively weak compared to - for example - the Christian god, who is &quot;more powerful than all of them combined.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with Abrahamic faith being a real thing in Scion, and having a real god backing it up. I'd be disappointed if it were otherwise. Makingany of them the <i>supreme</i> faith, however, strikes me as not being in the game's intended spirit.<br /> <br /> Monotheism just doesn't describe reality in Scion. There are monotheistic faiths and they believe in real gods, but the existence of other gods makes monotheism all too false.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-25-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:28:22-07:00","id":993100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993048#post993048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't find the idea of playing Scion in a Christian-centric universe to be appealing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps any, I don't consider the Abrahamic God above any others in Scion, but I think he should be just as real as any other. A Pantheon of one individual, Mantled at least three ways and caught between thousands of years of continuous Fatebinsings, and with a handful of Scions on the books, but ultimately on par with the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:31:12-07:00","id":993102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993100#post993100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it helps any, I don't consider the Abrahamic God above any others in Scion, but I think he should be just as real as any other. A Pantheon of one individual, Mantled at least three ways and caught between thousands of years of continuous Fatebinsings, and with a handful of Scions on the books, but ultimately on par with the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:11:52-07:00","id":993118,"title":"","content":"Can you get on board the notion that various Pantheons such as the Orisha or the Devas have a Primordial in their ranks, serving as a \u201cGreater God\u201d? Not all of them, to be sure; but many of them. <br /> <br /> If so, how about saying that monotheistic faiths in the World tend to be backed by suitable Primordials who <i>aren't</i> members of Pantheons? This sets the truth of the monotheistic faiths as being more henotheistic than monotheistic, as the existence of other gods is objectively true; but that still allows the Hebrew and Christian God to say \u201cyou shall have no other gods before me\u201d.<br /> <br /> This notion hinges on what Primordials are like. If they're as mysterious to the Gods as the Gods are to mortals, then it's possible that all Primordials are in fact different aspects of one being in a manner similar to mantling \u2014 or at least all Primordials who serve as the Godheads of monotheistic faiths and/or the \u201cGreater Gods\u201d of Pantheons who have such a thing. And mysterious Primordials are unlikely be active participants in Divine politics; if they were, they probably wouldn't be mysterious. So even if they technically have phenomenal cosmic power well beyond even the gods, Pantheons with a Primordial leader aren't going to have much more than an edge over Pantheons without one.<br /> <br /> This doesn't put Christianity at the center of Scion. Heck, it doesn't even put monotheistic faiths in a better position than polytheistic faiths, metaphysically speaking. It also doesn't make Christianity or Judaism any more true than any pantheistic faith; but its big advantage over other ways of handling the subject is that it doesn't make them any <i>less</i> true either.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the introduction of Primordials and Chosen Scions have gone a <i>long</i> way toward making <b>Scion</b> more accepting of non-pantheistic mythologies, monotheism included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:22:49-07:00","id":993121,"title":"","content":"I think that the idea of Primordials is where you'd find Abrahamic God, hanging out with other beings that are too big to manifest in the World. I don't think in power he'd be beyond other creator primordial entities, but I think any given one of them might be possessed of a bit more oomph than your random Raiden or Poseidon kind of deity, who is a being of a few specific things and comes in a nice comprehensible human like package.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:36:22-07:00","id":993132,"title":"","content":"Especially since 2e's don't have the \u201cevil enemies of the gods\u201d thing that 1e's Greater Titans had it makes them much more palatable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:39:15-07:00","id":993136,"title":"","content":"Oh, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> I more meant that is how someone who is monotheistic and a scion can believe without seeming insane. I agreed with others that they would seem insane and I think where we disagree is the part about Monotheism. If One God is only as powerful as one God from another pantheon who have an alliance than Monotheism just doesn't seem likely to spread. God faces off Jupiter while Mars/Neptune/Juno/etc get him from behind.<br /> <br /> On top of all that, any pantheon would have killed them just based on how much damage evangelicalism did to so many faiths. If Polytheism is True and Monotheism exists as a power in the world, than monotheism has to have weight. My idea would be Monotheism is more powerful (I mean look how much it has ravaged many Polytheistic faiths and seems dedicated to doing so, it doesn't do so as much here but still there's a reason it's number 1) but God rarely blesses anyone and mostly, does not answer prayers. <br /> <br /> Also, Monotheism has a place in so many mythologies, it seems a shame to call them all wrong. Say this God is a force that gets reinterpreted every way. Mortals made a faith that made them feel other gods weren't necessary trying to worship directly to this entity, but most Gods who do Worship this Deity feel they got it all wrong. In some ways I'm saying that Mythologies who have a monotheistic bent are right while the Abrahamic faiths are not. Still, by worshiping them Directly there is some protection that they get even the gods don't understand.<br /> <br /> In essence; the only way I see Monotheism still around without being declared the supreme religion with a supreme deity that actively stomps on the other gods, is if something special holds it back.<br /> <br /> Here's an idea, Monotheism are sorcerors stealing power from an almost Pantheistic deity, they first tied it to El, but the reason the religion spreads so far is God is everywhere and part of so many religions. All it takes is sincere belief in a one true God as a motif for these guys to steal the power. Without that extra buffer (the gods) Man kind of ran amuck without much to stop them. That doesn't mean these sorcerors are cruel or evil or do any of this on purpose, although some do. They appealed to a Deity, one even some gods had trouble fully understanding, and with that power spread their beliefs. Thus the very strong emphasis on faith. God still is very much real as a Christian/Muslim/Judaic figure since, y'know what it is as an almost Pantheistic god, but that isn't the only way to worship them, or even the one it is most active as. You believe in a supreme Deity that is this God, but whether Hindu, Persian, or Abrahamic they are a lot more complicated than meets the eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:41:15-07:00","id":993137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993050#post993050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How regular is regular though? 10 or so a generation? Which becomes a much smaller ratio as population grows, and similarly, less mythical events &quot;happen&quot;. And even then most scions never reach demi-god level, they instead become our De Vincis, our Hannibals, or our Beethovens. They are on the winning side of battles like Agincourt or New Orleans 1812. They are impressive and might alter events, but only a few will be known by more than a few hundred people. The core element here is that while there aren\u2019t any hard rules about not showing yourself, most tend to avoid the nasty fate entanglements, most periods of history don\u2019t have many, and most of those probably fade into folktales and urban legends. I think it is fairly easy to recontextualise events as \u201cthere was one at the one historical event\u201d well \u201cmaybe opposing ones canceled each other out\u201d, \u201cPantheon X didn\u2019t want to provoke a war with Pantheon y\u201d, \u201cNo one believed the witnesses\u201d, amd other perfectly believable excuses. If we assume that the cold war Neil has talked about has only been ramping up over the past couple decades than history probably wouldn\u2019t be massively changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I can't see even ten in a generation going unnoticed. They're going to be at the forefront of every major event just by dint of Fate making them go interesting places and that <i>can't</i> go unnoticed. Remember: Hannibal nearly brought Rome to its knees; Caesar destroyed an entire Pantheon; Christ and Mohammad both founded religious traditions that, at present, contain about half the entire populations of the planet.<br /> <br /> Imagine ten people like that every generation, with Fate bending to place them in just as grand a spotlight. How would our world survive it?<br /> <br /> This is without even entering into the sociocultural effects. I can't imagine there being a Reformation that split the Catholic and Protestant churches in a world that has far, far more polytheistic cults that are just as popular as the monotheistic ones. Monotheism won out over polytheism in our modern world but there's no reason for it to in Scion and quite possibly a large number of reason for it <i>not</i> to, as there are way more gods in a polytheistic pantheon than a monotheistic one. That's a lot more hands out there sprinkling the ichor.<br /> <br /> We are talking a world that might look a <i>bit</i> like our own, but only because a lot of the national boundaries we draw form from language and geographical barriers.<br /> <br /> The easiest answer to this is the most boring; to assume that there <i>aren't</i> any Scions we're unaware of in the background, bending the flow of history to their will, but rather that any given famous person of any import is in some way gifted with divine blood. Personally, though, while I would be truly enamoured with the French Cult of Reason managing to conjure a goddess who blessed Thomas &quot;A violent uprising every couple of decades is probably good for the country&quot; Jefferson, I don't <i>like</i> that idea for the same reason I don't like Big Man History; it's too simplistic and deprives the setting of feeling grand and mythical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:21:24-07:00","id":993185,"title":"","content":"Caesar actually achieved godhood, so did, theoretically at least, Christ and possibly Mohammad. They are the examples of some of the greatest heights a scion could achieve. The gods try not to act too overtly, they encourage their children to serve as covert agents to their agendas. We can see an uptick in, say, urban legends about a man in a tweed jacket and bowtie, but odds are no one can confirm anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:48:53-07:00","id":993193,"title":"","content":"Chances are the vast majority of Scions never leave Hero tier, and do extraordinary things that vanish into the ocean of history. A few years back a Gurkha stationed in Afghanistan fought off thirty Taliban by himself and while that's an incredible story, it's also already a footnote that most people will never, ever hear about. Thousands of really good fighters, healers, artists, friends of animals and the like really don't change the shape of history all that much.<br /> <br /> I doubt many Scions ever reach Demigod status, and so the rest are fated to be extraordinary people in their lifetimes that nobody ever hears about a century or two after their passing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:13:16-07:00","id":993205,"title":"","content":"The thing is, &quot;Fight off thirty people singlehandedly&quot; isn't something a Scion just does once in their entire life. It's something they do over and over and over again. It's something Fate will <i>make</i> them do over and over again because Fate wants them to be as balls-out interesting as possible, and it's something their divine patrons are going to keep poking them to do. &quot;Live in interesting times&quot; is a curse written into their very ichor.<br /> <br /> A Scion isn't going to be the sort of person who fights off thirty insurgent fighters in the desert and then goes back to an otherwise modestly impressive but mundane military career. They're the sort of person who keeps doing even <i>more</i> ludicrous stuff after that, over, and over, and over, because they are protagonists in the story. They're always at its centre. Scions don't get to do one big thing then retire; they've got to keep doing bigger and bigger things because that's how legends work.<br /> <br /> For a Scion, the Audie Murphy style &quot;Climb inside a burning gun wreck and fire it into a wall of tanks shooting at you with blood dripping across your eyes until you've driven them back, then walk away from the wreck before it explodes&quot; moment is just the beginning. After that, the Scion pretty much has to singlehandedly bash Hitler's head in with the giant concrete swastika torn from above the Reichstag.<br /> <br /> That's the take I've always seen in it, at least. And given that the example art shows a fire giant burning a city before a Scion comes riding a tidal wave to deliver a smackdown, I don't see how you <i>couldn't</i> have them bedecking the history books.<br /> <br /> &quot;That time D.C. was about to be obliterated by a giant until Teddy Roosevelt rode a giant moose straight into its gut&quot; is one of those things history remembers, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:39:36-07:00","id":993258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993205#post993205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, &quot;Fight off thirty people singlehandedly&quot; isn't something a Scion just does once in their entire life. It's something they do over and over and over again. It's something Fate will <i>make</i> them do over and over again because Fate wants them to be as balls-out interesting as possible, and it's something their divine patrons are going to keep poking them to do. &quot;Live in interesting times&quot; is a curse written into their very ichor.<br /> <br /> A Scion isn't going to be the sort of person who fights off thirty insurgent fighters in the desert and then goes back to an otherwise modestly impressive but mundane military career. They're the sort of person who keeps doing even <i>more</i> ludicrous stuff after that, over, and over, and over, because they are protagonists in the story. They're always at its centre. Scions don't get to do one big thing then retire; they've got to keep doing bigger and bigger things because that's how legends work.<br /> <br /> For a Scion, the Audie Murphy style &quot;Climb inside a burning gun wreck and fire it into a wall of tanks shooting at you with blood dripping across your eyes until you've driven them back, then walk away from the wreck before it explodes&quot; moment is just the beginning. After that, the Scion pretty much has to singlehandedly bash Hitler's head in with the giant concrete swastika torn from above the Reichstag.<br /> <br /> That's the take I've always seen in it, at least. And given that the example art shows a fire giant burning a city before a Scion comes riding a tidal wave to deliver a smackdown, I don't see how you <i>couldn't</i> have them bedecking the history books.<br /> <br /> &quot;That time D.C. was about to be obliterated by a giant until Teddy Roosevelt rode a giant moose straight into its gut&quot; is one of those things history remembers, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Atmajakki is right in her assessment that most scions don't make it past Hero - and they don't make it past Hero because they <i>die. </i>They don't go on to average military careers, Fate keeps putting them into combat situations and - because they're nod gods or even demigods yet - they take a bullet to the head and die. The alternative is to wonder why there aren't a whole hell-of-a-lot more demigods and gods running around. <br /> <br /> Also, I found your example for what Scions 'just start off doing' to be incredibly excessive, but I assume you were like - joking, because that's at least Demigod/God territory, not Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:59:40-07:00","id":993263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993258#post993258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Atmajakki is right in her assessment that most scions don't make it past Hero - and they don't make it past Hero because they <i>die. </i>They don't go on to average military careers, Fate keeps putting them into combat situations and - because they're nod gods or even demigods yet - they take a bullet to the head and die. The alternative is to wonder why there aren't a whole hell-of-a-lot more demigods and gods running around. <br /> <br /> Also, I found your example for what Scions 'just start off doing' to be incredibly excessive, but I assume you were like - joking, because that's at least Demigod/God territory, not Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. A Visitation is the magical equivalent of being handed a rifle; you can beat the holy hell out of folks that don't have a gun, but you'll have to be lucky or clever to beat someone trained with it - to say nothing of your odds of beating a tank in open combat. I guarantee the vast majority of people could be handed Legend 1 and a Purview to play with and still get our heads ripped off the first time we ever see a fire giant.<br /> <br /> Caesar conquered the Gauls and ascended to divinity, but I bet thousands of Scions of the Theoi died ingloriously in the trenches, wilds, arenas, and brothels of the Roman Empire, never to be heard from again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:24:28-07:00","id":993307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993258#post993258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I found your example for what Scions 'just start off doing' to be incredibly excessive, but I assume you were like - joking, because that's at least Demigod/God territory, not Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave three examples. Of these, two of them were things real, ordinary humans have done. I mean, we're using Julius Caesar as an example but JC was a real human being; flesh and blood that managed to commit mass genocide and enslavement by selective interpretation of a treaty with the Gallic tribes, all to pay his debts. In doing so, he was made a living god. All of that is what a mundane, fleshy mortal can do.<br /> <br /> Scions are a step above that.<br /> <br /> As for Roosevelt smashing a giant in the ghoulies with a bull moose, some of the example art for Hero has a character smashing a fire giant with a tidal wave. This is stuff the PCs are expected to be able to do at the Hero level. It may not be things they do right out of the gate, but it <i>is</i> the kind of thing the game expects you to get up to.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Caesar, let's assume most Scions do die. Does that change any of this? Julius Caesar's grand campaign is still being felt to this very day. His conquest of Britain obliterated British culture as it existed, introduced Christianity to the country, and gave Britain a context to frame its own imperial conquests more than a thousand years hence. The Roman Eagle found its way into the symbolism of just about every modern empire; all trying to make themselves into the New Rome.<br /> <br /> And this is without even touching things like the occasional giant attack tearing up a capital city or werewolves eating a king. Civil wars have spawned over less.<br /> <br /> There are so many elements here, I just cannot picture their world looking like ours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:30:06-07:00","id":993327,"title":"","content":"I would err on the side of Axelgear here, Heroic Scions, at least in 1e, are <i>incredibly powerful</i>. Through our play group's experiences in 1e, at Hero, Scions have accomplished the following off the top of my head.<ul><li>Leveled downtown Paris.</li> <li>Beat down a Legend 4 Heimdall at Legend 2. (Extraordinary dice rolls)</li> <li>Built and detonated Epic Int enhanced Nukes along a fault line, sinking the entirety of the British Isles, devastating the world economy and thrusting the world into chaos.</li> <li>Saved downtown New York by beating a Gorgon out on Epic Appearance, preventing anyone from looking at her.</li> <li>Talked down an enraged Ba'al and Yam before they threw down inside an urban center. Were manifestation as themselves, a colossal sea serpent for Yam's form.</li> <li>Surviving a massive explosion point blank without dodging that managed to almost biscect The Nuckelavee.</li> </ul>On a more conceptual level, I'll break down this a bit more into Physical, Social, and Mental Scions.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical</b> Scions in 1e could survive almost anything the mortal world threw at them. Armed with the Remington template, the best mortal (5 in Dexterity and Firearms. Remington +3) rolls 13 dice to hit. On average this will be 6.5 Successes, so, let's say 7 to be nice to them. The best Physical Scion at Legend 2 will defend against this with their Dodge Defense Value which is 8. (5 Dexterity, 5 Athletics, Epic Dexterity 1, and a basic Shield) So, on average the Mortal fails to hit by 1 and does nothing to the Scion. For this, let's say they got lucky and instead got 9 Successes, two above average, to hit with a Threshold of 1.<br /> <br /> Now the Mortal rolls Damage. They have 14 Dice (1 Threshold, 1 Base, 7 Remitting template damage, 5 Perception [This is technically a houserule, the only thing that adds to Damage is strength. But, this makes guns useless as they don't get an attribute. So, we'll give them Perception for damage.]) which will on average be 7 Successes. The Scion has the hide of a Nemean Lion since they are Theoi and rocking their Pantheon Pride. Therefore, the Scion has 12 Soak. (5 Stamina / 2 + Armor [8 Lethal], + Epic Stamina 1), and takes 0 damage.<br /> <br /> If this Scion were putting effort in, they can also chose to downgrade any Lethal Damage to Bashing for 1 Legend a piece, in which case their Bashing Soak is 13. Furthermore, once a Scene they can use Sophalistic Well Being and ignore any attack they were not directly aware of. Shoot them in the back of the head from point blank, shoot them with a battleship mounted railgun, they won't take a single point of damage. Additionally, they can use the Knacks Untouchable Opponent (with the nerf in place to prevent it from breaking everything) and Body Armor to bump their DDV and Soak up by 1 each.<br /> <br /> The Scion's values also improve as they get higher Legend to the following with these bonuses. Legend 3: DDV = 11 Soak = 13. Legend 4: DDV = 14, Soak = 16. Additionally, their ability to use their Knacks increases as their Legend pool becomes exponentially larger.<br /> <br /> <b>Social </b>is harder to look at with numbers, so, let's look at Knacks. Epic Charisma lets you make one person for 1 legend point totally invested in helping you, totally absolve yourself from blame (<i>and</i> also push this blame onto anyone else). Epic Manipulation make one person believe anything you say at all unless there is pure undeniable proof otherwise, as well as force one person to take one action immediately. Epic Appearance allows you to be so frightening you increase your DDV substantially.<br /> <br /> For a little focused study, we will look at the Manipulation Knack Trendsetter. You will be using this to cause a massive panic crash in the New York Stock Exchange, while you yourself profit infinitely through investments. This is a Manipulation + Presence roll, and let's say Legend 4 for this example, still Theoi. They have a pool of 14 dice and +4 Automatic Successes. On Average, you will get 11 Successes, which is 6 Successes higher than required to cause the entire population of New York to follow your trend. (which is making some horrific financial decision) The Social Scion is now vastly wealthy, and has brutalized the world economy for 2 Legend.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental</b> is even weirder to play with. But, first, let's look at the best possible mortal trying to invent something. They have 15 Dice (5 Int +5 Skill +5 Tool) to throw down, average of 8 rounded up. A Legend 4 Scion, still Theoi, gets to throw down 19 Dice and +4 Automatic Successes is 14 Successes. Add to this the Epic Intelligence Knack Math Genius, and Cypher, this Scion is also able to, making no rolls, solve every one of the Millennium Prize Problems in a matter of seconds, revolutionizing, like, everything. Also becoming a multi millionaire, but that's small bucks compared to our Epic Manipulation Scion above. Then with Cypher, you can rip through any form of computer security with no rolls in the blink of an eye, and make your own computer security that no mortal can ever solve ever in a million years ever.<br /> <br /> Then the Epic Perception Scions can also see really really far, but, that's not really dramatic.<br /> <br /> But, right. Hero Scions, at least in 1e, were world shakingly powerful. If you tried, you could bend the world around you. If 2e follows in a similar power scale, then a lot of Scions running around is probably not what's been going on. The kiddos are probably pretty rare. Especially because of the following: Scions are big risks. The Divine are investing a lot of time and effort into you, having Birthrights made, bound to you, and if you are a born Scion such all of 1e, having a child which they may have social obligations to. And then this Scion has a will of its own, it could try to end the world, or kill you, or rage against the heavens siding with Titans, or just be a <i>problem</i>. Scions are good things to keep low numbers of, they are <i>such </i>a hassle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 10-26-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:05:53-07:00","id":993388,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm of the opinion that Scions should be a relatively new development in the World that hasn't been around since the Gods were free intermingling with humanity eons ago. There's a couple exceptions like Julius Caesar but that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T06:05:04-07:00","id":993455,"title":"","content":"I see the art of fire giants and tidal waves in the middle of a city to be the once, maybe twice a millennia event. Most scions don't reach that point. They die as the rent a cop that singlehandedly stops a bank robbery of ten guys with body armor and AKs and then dies on the table afterwards. Even among scions the PCs are exceptional. In 1e most scions didn't even get birthrights before the titans escaped.<br /> <br /> The example of a mortal gunman against a physical scion is also ignoring things like onslaught penalties, coordinated assaults, and piercing damage. Heck most of those examples are more poor game balance than intentional awesomeness. Look in the 1e adversary section, a experienced cop is noted as being something a hero level scion should be concerned about tangling with. A swat team can and will pose a problem to any hero that isn't a legend four combat monkey.<br /> <br /> There are extraordinary people, some of them do extraordinary things that change the world, some do extraordinary things that get them fame in their time but are forgotten twenty years later, or fame in their fields, or turned into a local urban legend about some guy in a hopilite helmet that hurls muggers through brick walls and killed the heads of three different mob families. Just because you lead an interesting life doesn't mean people are going to hear about it or believe it if they do.<br /> <br /> I think Scions were certainly a very rare thing in ages past, and compounded with overly cautious parents, inter and intra pantheon politics, and a habit of getting into trouble probably lead to disgustingly high mortality rates. The likes of Hercules are remembered because they <i>won</i>. No one would care that he killed a hydra if someone did that two years earlier, they care because no one ever did it. I imagine there is going to be an in setting reason for the gods to be ramping up visitations and the handing out of birthrights in the modern day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:27:33-07:00","id":993565,"title":"","content":"&quot;The alternative is to wonder why there aren't a whole hell-of-a-lot more demigods and gods running around. &quot;<br /> <br /> To move up to Demigod and God requires certain things, many Scions who live to an ripe old age won't achieve it.<br /> <br /> We know know you have to die, likely in a Dramatic way to go from Demigod to God, and I wouldn't be surprised if there are otherwise other requirements for going from Hero to Demigod to God.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path also makes it clear that you never HAVE TO rise through the ranks, you can stay at Hero level forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:46:44-07:00","id":993579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993565#post993565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onyx Path also makes it clear that you never HAVE TO rise through the ranks, you can stay at Hero level forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only can you stay at Hero level forever, but 1E Raw even made allowances for going down in permanent legend if you lead a boring life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:52:13-07:00","id":993583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993455#post993455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the art of fire giants and tidal waves in the middle of a city to be the once, maybe twice a millennia event. Most scions don't reach that point. They die as the rent a cop that singlehandedly stops a bank robbery of ten guys with body armor and AKs and then dies on the table afterwards. Even among scions the PCs are exceptional. In 1e most scions didn't even get birthrights before the titans escaped.<br /> <br /> The example of a mortal gunman against a physical scion is also ignoring things like onslaught penalties, coordinated assaults, and piercing damage. Heck most of those examples are more poor game balance than intentional awesomeness. Look in the 1e adversary section, a experienced cop is noted as being something a hero level scion should be concerned about tangling with. A swat team can and will pose a problem to any hero that isn't a legend four combat monkey.<br /> <br /> There are extraordinary people, some of them do extraordinary things that change the world, some do extraordinary things that get them fame in their time but are forgotten twenty years later, or fame in their fields, or turned into a local urban legend about some guy in a hopilite helmet that hurls muggers through brick walls and killed the heads of three different mob families. Just because you lead an interesting life doesn't mean people are going to hear about it or believe it if they do.<br /> <br /> I think Scions were certainly a very rare thing in ages past, and compounded with overly cautious parents, inter and intra pantheon politics, and a habit of getting into trouble probably lead to disgustingly high mortality rates. The likes of Hercules are remembered because they <i>won</i>. No one would care that he killed a hydra if someone did that two years earlier, they care because no one ever did it. I imagine there is going to be an in setting reason for the gods to be ramping up visitations and the handing out of birthrights in the modern day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, because whatever the Watcher offers up as an example, his player group is clearly tailor made to accomplish the things they are attempting to accomplish, rather than being developed with a Simulationist or Narrativist agenda. Likewise with Axelgear - the source of my umbrage with what you said is that you actively sought to <i>trivialize</i> acts of heroism, that is not what the game is supposed to be about. They are meant to feel epic and meaningful, not just 'that thing every Scion starts off doing'. <br /> <br /> Actual Scions don't have a wealth of experience with the game and all its mechanisms, they don't build themselves to be good at shooting things, or surviving explosions, or the perfect combination to steal nukes, get them in the right areas without being caught, and then set them off. Which is why the player character Scions are so often more powerful than npc Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:01:28-07:00","id":993621,"title":"","content":"Where did I trivialize acts of heroism? I am disagreeing with the concept that the existence of scions would have a dramatic effect on history, and I'm doing so by pointing out that, even in the mythical times of Hercules, Odyssyues, and the Argonauts, the acts they performed <i>were</i> Epic and meaningful. If any scion could do what they did it wouldn't be legendary because every scion would start off doing it. And that the PCs can do the same is proof they are destined for great things. PC scions aren't more powerful than NPC scions because of the magic of metagaming, they are stronger because they are fated for great things, to reach heights even most other Heroes never reach.<br /> <br /> And my other point about actions going unnoticed. That doesn't mean they aren't epic and meaningful, it just means that when your band stops a small army of fire giants from setting off the yellowstone super volcano that most people aren't going to know that. You still saved millions of lives, and people in the supernatural community are probably going to hear about it, but unless the scions come forward with some irrefutable evidence humanity at large will never know or believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:26:15-07:00","id":993630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993621#post993621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did I trivialize acts of heroism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solana was addressing axelgear with that comment about trivializing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:12:30-07:00","id":993659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993583#post993583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, because whatever the Watcher offers up as an example, his player group is clearly tailor made to accomplish the things they are attempting to accomplish, rather than being developed with a Simulationist or Narrativist agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you meant that to come off as dismissive as it did, that is a pretty harsh accusation. Those characters were not tailor made to acomplish the things they were attempting to acomplish at all. I know for sure that at least two of them were for sure developed with a narrativist agenda, people first and foremost, not min maxed for specific things, since I was the one who made them. The Scion who survived the explosion had a single Dot of Epic Stamina, no armor, no nothing, I just blew almost all of my resources to hang on at all Agg except Lethal on Incap. He was a Thief and Investigator, not built to survive explosions at all. I spent the entire next story avoiding taking even a single point of damage least I simply just die. Leveling downtown Paris was Social Scions miscalculating something, they didn't actually <i>intend</i> to level the city. A party got out of hand.<br /> <br /> I will agree that Physical Scions are weak at Hero. But, you don't have to be built to break the world to do so with Socials or Mentals in 1e. Math Genius is from Scion: Hero, and has no prerequisite. It isn't something like digging through sourcebooks for obscure things, or having two strange powers interact in an odd way. If you hit Legend 4 and had max Epic Int, you <i>had </i>to have 3 Knacks from Epic Int. There were 5 options, if you were only playing with Scion: Hero, one of which was Math Genius. You only had three options if your ST removed the experience cost changing Knacks because they made the game wonky.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of this discussion comes down to personal preference in how you run games. There isn't really a right answer. Vonpenguin is bang on that there is inconsistencies in what 1e says and what 1e does. Physically, Heroes should not be able to fight regiments, and can't due to the mass combat or assist stacking rules. The number of Scions in the world in our games tends to be low for social reasons on the part of the Gods. Sure, the kid is mortal, but social systems still exist which make it complicated. If Lugh's son is murdered during a dinner at a foreign embassy, Lugh will be culturally compelled to bring wrath and ruin down on those involved, and that's a lot of effort for a God, especially when interacting with the world is the sort of thing they don't want to do.<br /> <br /> However, at the same time, I have played in other games where Heroes were numerous. Not thousands, but a couple hundred on the planet at once during the Titan War. In that setting, the Gods didn't oblige the social relationships with the kiddos just because they couldn't really. They were at war, a suspension of social obligations and the sort. Or, for some Pantheons, Scions, being Mortals, were not really <i>people</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:08:28-07:00","id":993692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993659#post993659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you meant that to come off as dismissive as it did, that is a pretty harsh accusation. Those characters were not tailor made to acomplish the things they were attempting to acomplish at all. I know for sure that at least two of them were for sure developed with a narrativist agenda, people first and foremost, not min maxed for specific things, since I was the one who made them. The Scion who survived the explosion had a single Dot of Epic Stamina, no armor, no nothing, I just blew almost all of my resources to hang on at all Agg except Lethal on Incap. He was a Thief and Investigator, not built to survive explosions at all. I spent the entire next story avoiding taking even a single point of damage least I simply just die. Leveling downtown Paris was Social Scions miscalculating something, they didn't actually <i>intend</i> to level the city. A party got out of hand.<br /> <br /> I will agree that Physical Scions are weak at Hero. But, you don't have to be built to break the world to do so with Socials or Mentals in 1e. Math Genius is from Scion: Hero, and has no prerequisite. It isn't something like digging through sourcebooks for obscure things, or having two strange powers interact in an odd way. If you hit Legend 4 and had max Epic Int, you <i>had </i>to have 3 Knacks from Epic Int. There were 5 options, if you were only playing with Scion: Hero, one of which was Math Genius. You only had three options if your ST removed the experience cost changing Knacks because they made the game wonky.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of this discussion comes down to personal preference in how you run games. There isn't really a right answer. Vonpenguin is bang on that there is inconsistencies in what 1e says and what 1e does. Physically, Heroes should not be able to fight regiments, and can't due to the mass combat or assist stacking rules. The number of Scions in the world in our games tends to be low for social reasons on the part of the Gods. Sure, the kid is mortal, but social systems still exist which make it complicated. If Lugh's son is murdered during a dinner at a foreign embassy, Lugh will be culturally compelled to bring wrath and ruin down on those involved, and that's a lot of effort for a God, especially when interacting with the world is the sort of thing they don't want to do.<br /> <br /> However, at the same time, I have played in other games where Heroes were numerous. Not thousands, but a couple hundred on the planet at once during the Titan War. In that setting, the Gods didn't oblige the social relationships with the kiddos just because they couldn't really. They were at war, a suspension of social obligations and the sort. Or, for some Pantheons, Scions, being Mortals, were not really <i>people</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that I hadn't intended to sound elitest, dismissive, or offensive. But certainly it doesn't approach anything my group ever managed to accomplish when we played 1e Scion. I apologize for my impudence. Truth be told I was just getting a bit defensive over how Axelgear was voicing his opinions, coupled with the way my social circles always have that one person who will know the game and its mechanics better than everyone else - so even if they're not approaching it from a Gamist perspective, they know how to make a stronger character than say, someone who 'wants' to make a mental social character for the first time, and just sort of plays things by ear. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:03:56-07:00","id":993754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993455#post993455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the art of fire giants and tidal waves in the middle of a city to be the once, maybe twice a millennia event. Most scions don't reach that point. They die as the rent a cop that singlehandedly stops a bank robbery of ten guys with body armor and AKs and then dies on the table afterwards. Even among scions the PCs are exceptional. In 1e most scions didn't even get birthrights before the titans escaped.<br /> <br /> The example of a mortal gunman against a physical scion is also ignoring things like onslaught penalties, coordinated assaults, and piercing damage. Heck most of those examples are more poor game balance than intentional awesomeness. Look in the 1e adversary section, a experienced cop is noted as being something a hero level scion should be concerned about tangling with. A swat team can and will pose a problem to any hero that isn't a legend four combat monkey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that example art is usually intended as a thing players will get to do, I somehow get the feeling it isn't intended as something that <i>maybe</i> happens once a millennium, especially given that the tidal wave power is a starting ability for Heroic Scions. Even if it <i>did</i> only happen that rarely, though, that is well and truly enough to reshape history. The further back you go, the more it reshapes it.<br /> <br /> You're also making the assumption that, because we used militaristic Scions as an example thus far, they're the <i>only</i> Scions that can change the world and that simply is not the case.<br /> <br /> Consider, for example, the Printing Press; a deceptively simple invention which reshaped the ancient world into the modern world in the span of a handful of centuries. China had the printing press centuries before Europe ever did but made little use of it because of the complexity of the Chinese alphabet. Yet we have Scions; the superior geniuses whose brilliance can turn out radical new inventions. What if one of them looks at a wine press and skips Gutenberg by a few dozen generations? Imagine widespread writing in the 4th century. One little tweak and the world becomes unrecognizable.<br /> <br /> Or what about charismatic Scions? Consider, for example, the fiery Martin Luther, who bent European religion over his knee without even intending it. What happens when the pre-Christian religions have <i>their</i> Peters? Their Pauls? What happens when these charismatic evangelists cause a spiritual reshaping and revival of their old faiths? And then, what follows when all the religious wars that shaped the modern world took an entirely different shape?<br /> <br /> What happens if a Catholic Scion kept the Dutch Republic Catholic with their fanatical speeches? Without that, there's no Eighty Years War, no Protestant arm besides that of England trying to force the Peace of Westphalia, no safe haven for Lutherans and Calvinists, no birth of the Dutch Enlightenment...<br /> <br /> And even if you consider those to be the &quot;big&quot;, rare Scions, I'd say you only need one of the above examples and the world is a completely different place.<br /> <br /> But what about the small ones? Consider, then, all the small parts played by people in history that have added up to big deals. Consider, for example, how history might have played out if Simon Bolivar's would-be assassin in Jamaica had possessed the spoiled Hunter Knacks that let you better track your target. A knife in the man's heart and the South American resistance to Spain literally dies in its bed.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps the physician who has that little bit of magic that keeps a suitably important person from dying, like, say, Nicholas Hartwig. A Scion who can save a man from a heart attack in 1913 prevents the First World War singlehandedly and, with it, the entire reshaping of the map as we know it today.<br /> <br /> History is such a big, messy thing. I can't see how introducing the possibility of giants smushing cities or people with the power to raise the dead into the mix <i>can't</i> utterly twist and blend it beyond recognition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993583#post993583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, because whatever the Watcher offers up as an example, his player group is clearly tailor made to accomplish the things they are attempting to accomplish, rather than being developed with a Simulationist or Narrativist agenda. Likewise with Axelgear - the source of my umbrage with what you said is that you actively sought to <i>trivialize</i> acts of heroism, that is not what the game is supposed to be about. They are meant to feel epic and meaningful, not just 'that thing every Scion starts off doing'.<br /> <br /> Actual Scions don't have a wealth of experience with the game and all its mechanisms, they don't build themselves to be good at shooting things, or surviving explosions, or the perfect combination to steal nukes, get them in the right areas without being caught, and then set them off. Which is why the player character Scions are so often more powerful than npc Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't stop you from seeing that as trivializing. If you think a Scion who, for the first time, singlehandedly holds off thirty people, even when they have superlative combat skills, does not come out of it feeling like a monster truck that walks like a man, that's your deal. Me, personally, I would see that as a character-defining moment that causes them to realize just what kind of creature they've become; the moment where they feel divinity coursing through their veins and ride whatever powerful, heady feelings surge through them. Maybe they break down and cry, thinking they're a monster; maybe they elate and laugh madly as they savour this adrenaline-fueled sensation of victory. Maybe somewhere in-between.<br /> <br /> But in the end, epic things are what Scions do because they are Scions. It might take them a little while to get there but it is emphatically <i>what they do</i>. Scion is a game of Epic Storytelling and epic stories include things like Achilles standing naked on a hill, shouting at an army in rage and grief. Prince Rama hunts demons as a teenager. Samson beats thirty men to death because he's feeling a little pissy and a thousand when he truly gets mad. Hercules slays a lion with his bare hands as a warm-up.<br /> <br /> Do these stories trivialize these events? Goodness, no. They build up to them first but they all <i>happen</i>. That's the point. Scions are <i>supposed</i> to do this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> If you envision a world where Scions don't do the very thing they're supposed to do, what sort of thing do you envision happening? Scions don't <i>need</i> to start out perfect to do these things (though many of them are already exceptional by dint of divine blood), but they <i>will</i> do them with time and they will just keep getting better in the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993692#post993692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right that I hadn't intended to sound elitest, dismissive, or offensive. But certainly it doesn't approach anything my group ever managed to accomplish when we played 1e Scion. I apologize for my impudence. Truth be told I was just getting a bit defensive over how Axelgear was voicing his opinions, coupled with the way my social circles always have that one person who will know the game and its mechanics better than everyone else - so even if they're not approaching it from a Gamist perspective, they know how to make a stronger character than say, someone who 'wants' to make a mental social character for the first time, and just sort of plays things by ear.</div> </div> </div> </div>We all get upset from time to time. I'm stating my opinions pretty strongly, which can be pretty abrasive, so I apologize for any discomfort I've caused.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I <i>don't</i> create my characters to game the system; the only game I get to play in regularly, my character's a Thyrsus whose biggest area of specialty is singing because that felt to fit the character the most. Doesn't exactly help you fight werewolves, though, does it?<br /> <br /> Characters in games will meet challenges they're capable of overcoming, though, because that's how games work. The Storyteller takes the role of Fate, helping create a legend. PCs are usually expected to be at least somewhat exceptional, but if they're all super-special-awesome by default, it makes them not feel like a part of the world. Scions should all be epic to my mind.<br /> <br /> ... Phew. That was a lot to get out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:12:42-07:00","id":993763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993754#post993754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all get upset from time to time. I'm stating my opinions pretty strongly, which can be pretty abrasive, so I apologize for any discomfort I've caused.<br /> <br /> As it stands, I <i>don't</i> create my characters to game the system; the only game I get to play in regularly, my character's a Thyrsus whose biggest area of specialty is singing because that felt to fit the character the most. Doesn't exactly help you fight werewolves, though, does it?<br /> <br /> Characters in games will meet challenges they're capable of overcoming, though, because that's how games work. The Storyteller takes the role of Fate, helping create a legend. PCs are usually expected to be at least somewhat exceptional, but if they're all super-special-awesome by default, it makes them not feel like a part of the world. Scions should all be epic to my mind.<br /> <br /> ... Phew. That was a lot to get out.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I'm most concerned about when playing or running Scion is keeping it from feeling too much like it covers the same creative space as Exalted, which a few of the examples listed felt it was approaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:43:58-07:00","id":993773,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I don't think that's something you can avoid. Scion and Exalted have the same essential source material; they're both calling on things like the Ramayana, the Bible, the Iliad, Journey to the West, etc. Hercules is the archetypal Dawn <i>and</i> a solid example character for a Scion.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm more than happy to explore it. What creative space would you prefer to see Scion cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:04:45-07:00","id":993785,"title":"","content":"Not going to directly quote things for length but, mental and social scions can definitely change the world, and likely have done so. But the same way the marvel setting isn't filled with perfect medicine, clean energy for all, and a full on post scarcity society even though they have people like Reed Richards and Tony Stark running around, you have to assume that what the scions do, they do in a way that ends with an Earth that is recognizable as Earth. Maybe a scion manipulates things behind the scenes and starts an extra crusade, or a social scion talks john wilkes booth out of assassinating Lincoln, these are major, major events, but would they really change our modern landscape that much? Probably not. This is an alternate universe, we can say that x happened because there was a scion involved, or justify why a scion wasn't involved by saying another scion interfered.<br /> <br /> And I think the core problem here is, you are talking about how Scions are led to great things, and that is 100% true, but only the ones that survive become legends. Achilles was nearly invulnerable, something no other heroes of Greek myth can claim, it makes him stand out head and shoulders, but the scion of Ares that ran into a veteran Achilles during his first post visitation battle won't be remembered by anyone.<br /> <br /> And while the art implies it is something the players will do, doesn't imply it is something that is remotely close to <i>common</i> in the setting. Player characters do cool things because it is their story, and their story is meant to be on on the scale of all the figures mentioned. But most scions won't fly that high. So it wouldn't be common knowledge that the gods and legendary creatures are real. Governments probably know, certain figures in academic circles might know, but telling the public at large would be career suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T18:56:31-07:00","id":993824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993773#post993773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I don't think that's something you can avoid. Scion and Exalted have the same essential source material; they're both calling on things like the Ramayana, the Bible, the Iliad, Journey to the West, etc. Hercules is the archetypal Dawn <i>and</i> a solid example character for a Scion.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm more than happy to explore it. What creative space would you prefer to see Scion cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with Scion getting into Exalted space at the Demigod/God level, Origin/Hero not so much. I really don't want to use poor examples, but sort of the first things that come to mind for Hero power level would be like the Lord of the Rings films (as opposed to the books, and especially the Silmarillion, a lot of that is probably more Demigod level?), Daredevil, Jessica Jones, that sort of pay grade, maybe a bit of Supernatural on the less flashy end? At Demigod maybe you branch a bit into Methuselah, like in that 2014 Noah film? (Arguably the only good part of it, really.) Or Equilibrium, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Later-end of Demigod and into god would be much closer to The Avengers/Exalted I would think, none of my games ever actually got that far in, but as I understand it by the time you're that powerful, you're more confined to the Overworld than you are to The World, so you wouldn't be sinking a landmass, anyway. Not directly anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:07:17-07:00","id":993831,"title":"","content":"The one thing I want to point out to everyone: we've seen what Heroes can do in 2e in at least one regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Changing Tides</b><br /><br /> Cost: Imbue 1 Legend or Spend 1 Legend <br /> Duration: One scene or Instant <br /> Subject: Body of water <br /> Range: Long <br /> Action: Simple <br /> You exert your will over water, controlling the tides or currents that move through it. You can calm all water out to long range, making it still and placid even in the face of a hurricane, or change the direction that currents flow in, letting you reverse the direction of a river or cause a riptide to drag lost swimmers back to shore. <br /> Alternatively, if you spend Legend instead of imbuing it, you can call up a great wave to crash down on your foes. You roll this attack with (highest Power Attribute) + Occult and Enhancement 4. It has the shockwave tag (p. XX), letting you attack all characters in a single range band within long range, as well as the bashing and pushing tags. </div> </div> </div> So for anyone saying that Scions should all be reshaping history and massively wrecking things... it takes the only dot of Legend a starting Scion has to make one pretty big wave. You can do a lot with that, sure, and it's definitely a noteworthy event... but it's also less destructive than a single artillery shot. Heroes are largely bound to the realm of the extraordinary but largely human with what they can do, and by the time you get up to the real heavy lifting that's when Fate starts slapping you down for making so many ripples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:13:10-07:00","id":993855,"title":"","content":"Edit: Might've misunderstood. Re-checking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 10-26-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:17:46-07:00","id":993857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993855#post993855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;All characters in a single range band within long range&quot; means you can hit everything out to &quot;maximum effective range&quot;, of which the standard is one kilometer. If I were to, say, target the city I grew up in with such an attack from the harbour front, I could reasonably hope to seriously injure about 5,000 people.<br /> <br /> That is a hit comparable to the Halifax Explosion, one of the largest non-nuclear blasts in recorded history.<br /> <br /> Now, don't get me wrong: Fate would be standing there with a very large chopping knife and a really nasty look in its eye, but that this is something a Scion can do from the word &quot;go&quot; is... Well, it's a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>All people within a single range band (within a long range of where you currently are) is 5,000 people? That's a densely packed community. It's also Bashing, and probably wouldn't destroy the buildings or anything like that.<br /> <br /> Edit: There doesn't seem to be an option to delete this post, in light of you double checking. : \\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-26-2016, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:19:55-07:00","id":993858,"title":"","content":"I think you're drastically overstating the area of that.<br /> <br /> It's <i>a single range band</i>, out to long-range,-- i.e., if the range bands are &quot;Close, Short, Medium, Long, and Extreme&quot; then you could hit ONE of those range bands with your wave. I.e., you could aim at a stretch of road that's a Long distance away from you and hit everything within 'one range band' at that location. But, you're NOT sending your wave roaring through the entire encompassed space between you and that stretch of road. The area of effect is impressive but not overwhelming.<br /> <br /> It's more equivalent to, say, a bridge being washed out. If I had to guess. But, we don't really have enough information to gauge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:21:56-07:00","id":993859,"title":"","content":"Now, in my defense, the language there is really contorted. But yeah, I saw my mistake.<br /> <br /> Still think that Scions would fuck shit up, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:24:59-07:00","id":993861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=993859#post993859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, in my defense, the language there is really contorted. But yeah, I saw my mistake.<br /> <br /> Still think that Scions would fuck shit up, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I've shown you using the only glimpse of the rules I have so far that they don't until much higher Legend, likely so much so that they're Demigods. Everything we've seen so far suggests that Heroes aren't going to do terribly much more than any extraordinary mortal to start off with and have to contest with exponentially nastier threats than anyone out of our histories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:34:21-07:00","id":993863,"title":"","content":"You have? Has any of what you said contradicted what I've said previously? Scions not being able to level cities with a gesture from the word go doesn't change that they are still modestly superhuman just to begin with and only get more so with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:40:15-07:00","id":993865,"title":"","content":"I sure do love this conversation about Monotheism, this thread's topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T21:13:12-07:00","id":993876,"title":"","content":"It <i>was</i> on-topic; discussing whether anything like monotheism could exist in a setting with Scions. Still, as you say, we've sorta burned through that, so on to a more fun turn of the page.<br /> <br /> I'd probably play monotheism in any game of Scion as being treated in one of two ways, depending on what form it takes.<br /> <br /> Monotheism that says there is only one god or that one god is supreme over all others will get treated like the Romans treated it; as superstition. Not in the modern sense of the world, but as something you can do but which is largely unnecessary. Having a particularly close connection with a god is normal, but treating them as the be-all and end-all is overboard.<br /> <br /> The other, more Brahmist interpretation is that the gods are all facets of some supreme but distant overdeity, which rules beyond even the highest heaven. That sort of belief is pretty compatible with other beliefs. Depending on circumstances, it might brush over into a violent fundamentalism, but that's really dependent on the type(s) of story I want to tell at a given time.<br /> <br /> That said, just as many Catholics are most familiar with a particular saint, so likely are most people familiar with a particular patron deity, which would give rise to a diversity of traditions. The World, as I see it, would more resemble the traditional religious practices of India - a great diversity, with more focus on what your beliefs lead you to do than what gods you believe in - than the monotheistic practices that arose in the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T21:00:56-07:00","id":994390,"title":"","content":"I often go with the notion that there is no Overdeity - every god and every person is a unique, yet connected entity that collectively make up that original singular unity.<br /> <br /> If you've ever read Alan Moore's Promethea, itself an inspiration for Mage: the Awakening, that's basically what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T23:26:23-08:00","id":1009650,"title":"","content":"Sorry for resurrecting this thread, but I feel like sharing <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modekngei\" target=\"_blank\">Modekngei</a>. I imagine that there would be a multitude of similar religions in the Scion version of the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 11-29-2016, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:30:29-08:00","id":1009664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=1009650#post1009650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for ressurecting this thread, but I feel like sharing <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modekngei\" target=\"_blank\">Modekngei</a>, which I imagine the Scion version of the World would have a lot more similar religions too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well most of the monotheists I know think Resurection is great.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The sea looks at the stability of the mountain and sighs. The mountain watches the freedom of the sea and cries.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11634-sea-envy","name":"Sea-Envy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11634_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T14:58:59-08:00","id":1010352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=977414#post977414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's 9. The first three are mentioned in the Bible proper, while the next five are listed in the Book of Enoch. Metatron is more of a mystery and seems more tied to the Talmud. Reviewing the original Scion game, the pantheons ranged from 12 at the most to as little as 7. So, technically, you have a full roster right there. There is another list that has Jophiel, Zadkiel, and Camael for other additions or alternate names for the first nine. And, of course, more could be added, either from In Nominee or just coming up with more on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>On names, I recommend <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Dictionary-Angels-Including-Fallen/dp/002907052X\" target=\"_blank\">A Dictionary of Angels</a>. Lots of info and cross references if you want to dive into the angelology rabbit hole. The intro covers methodology and processes, as well as the Lucifer debate. (Specifically if he exists or happens to be religious fan fiction due to a mistranslation or misinterpretation of the Bible.) It's a thick book and a purchase I love. It's come in handy for a number of games.<br /> <br /> More on topic, I'm inclined towards God/YHWH/Allah being a mystery in setting and a matter of faith. Angels, saints, demons/fallen angels, etc exist and they do whatever it is they do. Every once in a while angels perform their role as messengers announcing 'you're a Scion' and that results in saints, prophets, Nephilim, and the like. Historically this has resulted in notable Scions/Prophets like Jesus and Mohammad. When asked about God, the angels make it a matter of faith, but don't address the question directly because of reasons of faith and they don't want to spill that God/YHWH/Allah is too fatebound to act. The average PC's best case scenario: &quot;Sorry, He's busy. I'll take Him a message. It's what angels do.&quot; On no account will the Scion get an audience. Is He a Titan, Primordial, or Overgod? No one knows outside of the upper echelons of the Host and they aren't talking. It's a need to know basis, and you don't need to know unless your GM thinks otherwise.<br /> <br /> When asked about the other pantheons, the Host's answer is that the 'gods' are powerful entities, but they are no more 'gods' than angels are. (Despite what their followers think.) Some 'gods' might be considered demons, some aren't. The attitude of the Host resulted in historical conflict and animosity especially after Christianity and Islam flourished. Right now there's a bit of a detente.<br /> <br /> Due to the current (RL) fighting between the various Abrahamic religious sects, the Host is in a state of civil war. The other Pantheons have had a bit of freedom since they don't have to deal with the Host(s). I vaguely remember from somewhere that a couple of the archangels are direct patrons of specific Abrahamic religions, so that could be the source of the conflict. If you really want to emphasize the civil war, some of the gods could be antagonizing the Host(s) so the civil war continues. Then the gods get the breathing room they need to accomplish their goals without the Host(s) interference. Tons of plot hooks for all sorts of PCs there.<br /> <br /> Mechanically God/YHWH/Allah has no stats. The angels, saints, prophets, etc are represented by the appropriate Legend and are treated mechanically as gods, even though they aren't in setting. Angels and so on are simply imbued with His Grace and the mechanics represent His relative investiture. Scions are of the appropriate type happen now and again and progress just as any other Scion does.<br /> <br /> In game, relevance is left to the table/GM to decide. PC Scions of the Host can play nice just fine based on motivation and shared PC goals. (PCs generally don't want demons/monsters destroying downtown.) NPC Scions might demonstrate the worst extremes of the Abrahamic religions fighting both external and internal heretics.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> -Ariketh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":753,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","user":"Ariketh","date":". 11-30-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T16:30:01-08:00","id":1010395,"title":"","content":"For the most part, I like it. However, I would say that there are almost no Abrahamic Scions, per se. Followers of Abrahamic faiths basically fall into two categories: humans (who operate the Origins and Hero tiers) and angels (who operate in the Demigod and God tiers). The line between Hero and Demigod is never crossed, the only exception maybe being the Nephilim. But for the most part, plan for a Scion game that includes Abrahamic protagonists to stay in a given tier indefinitely.<br /> <br /> Traditionally, humans have almost always operated at the Origins tier, the most notable exception being Samson. But traditionally, they haven't been sharing a world with Heroes and Demigods. In a world where the enemies of the Abrahamic faiths regularly field such beings, there are more occasions where Samson-like Heroes will be raised up to defend the faith. Meanwhile, angels normally operate on the Demigod tier, with a select few of them (Michael, Gabriel, Lucifer, etc.) operating on the level of gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:45:40-08:00","id":1010423,"title":"","content":"In my version of the World, YHWH and his angels are something of a conspiracy theory among divine beings -- the equivalent of UFOs or the Illuminati. None of the major pantheons have ever encountered either directly, and most deny their existence. Of course, mortal worshipers of the Abrahamic God are almost as common as they are in our world, but these days they're mostly too focused on fighting among themselves to pose much of a threat to &quot;idolaters.&quot; That said, a few pantheons have had unpleasant run-ins with Prophets or Saints claiming to serve the Most High. The Netjer Do Not Talk About Moses, and the Arabic 'Alihah still haven't recovered from what Muhammad and his companions did to them. The Canaanite Elohim are rumored to know more, but they're not talking -- in fact, they won't even say His name out loud. Those deities who do believe in YHWH's existence often become paranoid and obsessed with deciphering His hidden agenda, often seeing Him as the secret mastermind behind Titanic activity, inter-pantheon conflict, and other threats. Angel sightings, real or fake, are a common topic of discussion on divine message boards. There's also a growing community of &quot;Armageddon preppers,&quot; making ready for the day when the Heavenly Host finally come for them. After all, if YHWH does exist, the one thing anyone knows for certain is that He's a <i>jealous</i> God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:46:09-08:00","id":1010425,"title":"","content":"I've said elsewhere that my personal solution to where the Abrahamic faiths fit into Scion's World in terms of having mojo to throw around is by having an Angelic Pantheon that almost exclusively creates Chosen Scions or else handles things themselves, and then that a great number of mortals use Abrahamic motifs to work their magics as miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T23:52:49-08:00","id":1010538,"title":"","content":"I think it would be more interesting to have a Demonic pantheon than an Angelic one. I mean, yeah sure, you could have Gabriel as your parent.... or you could have the motherfucking Leviathan.<br /> <br /> Besides, a Demonic pantheon would probably be less likely to offend people and, at least in my opinion, would be easier to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T23:55:39-08:00","id":1010539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism?p=1010538#post1010538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be more interesting to have a Demonic pantheon than an Angelic one. I mean, yeah sure, you could have Gabriel as your parent.... or you could have the motherfucking Leviathan.<br /> <br /> Besides, a Demonic pantheon would probably be less likely to offend people and, at least in my opinion, would be easier to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like an Angelic Pantheon solely because you could explore different readings of them between faiths and also draw on their later symbolism in other occult traditions, like Dee's writings on associating the archangels to the planets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}